Wedding plans shift close to the date. Guest counts move, the weather turns, and sometimes the date itself changes. Malaga Event Gear (MEG) supplies the AV side of a wedding only, sound, microphones, lighting, and a technician on the packages that include one, so this guide covers what actually happens to that AV booking when something changes late, governed by our real 24 hour minimum notice policy. For the full picture of what we cover for weddings, see our [wedding rentals](/blog/wedding-rentals/) overview.

## Brief Overview

---

MEG's one hard rule for late changes is the 24 hour minimum notice: every booking, and every change to a booking, needs that window to guarantee scheduling and equipment availability. Inside that window most changes are possible, but none of them are guaranteed. Availability, not price, is what is actually at risk close to the date. A guest count that crosses the [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) (up to 50) or [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) (up to 80) threshold means switching packages, not adjusting a quantity. Add ons, a projector, a smoke machine, an extra microphone, extra technician hours, can usually be requested late, subject to what is still in stock and who is still free. Date changes and a weather driven indoor to outdoor swap are the two changes most likely to run into a wall, since a technician and equipment already committed to your original date, or configured for one setting, cannot be reassigned by a promise alone.

## Key Highlights

---

-   The 24 hour minimum notice policy applies to every booking and every change to one. There is no exception for a last minute request.
-   Guest count crossing 50 (Eco Pack) or 80 (Wedding Pack) after booking is a package change, not a quantity tweak, and it is subject to availability.
-   Add ons, a projector and screen, a smoke machine, extra microphones, extra technician hours, can be requested close to the date, but each is confirmed against real stock and technician time, not guaranteed on request.
-   A date change risks a double booked technician or a peak season date that is already gone. There is no documented rush fee, but there is also no guaranteed availability.
-   Package prices are fixed. A smaller guest count after booking does not lower what you already booked.

## The 24 Hour Minimum Notice Is a Hard Floor

Every event gear rental and technical service with MEG must be contracted with a minimum of 24 hours' advance notice, to guarantee scheduling and logistical availability. That rule does not stop applying once you have already booked. A change request, a bigger guest count, a new add on, a different date, a different venue, needs to clear the same 24 hour window before we can confirm it. It is not a soft guideline we bend for a good reason. It is the floor every request is checked against, whether it is your first booking or a change to one you already made. For large or complex changes, reaching out as early as possible is what actually protects your date, not the 24 hours themselves, which are a minimum, not a target.

## Guest Count Crossing a Package Threshold

The [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) is built for up to 50 guests and runs self operated after our crew installs and tests it. The [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) is built for up to 80 guests and includes a live technician throughout the event. If your final guest count rises past 50 on an Eco Pack booking close to the date, that is not a quantity you can simply add to. It is a switch to a different, higher capacity system, and on the Wedding Pack specifically, a technician to run it. Confirming that switch depends on whether the larger system and, if needed, a technician are still free for your date, and it is still bound by the 24 hour minimum. The reverse does not create a discount: if your guest count drops after booking, the package price you already confirmed does not change. Our [tips for reducing wedding rental costs](/blog/tips-for-reducing-wedding-rental-costs/) guide covers why right sizing the package before you book, not after, is the real lever.

<InlineCTA />

## Adding an Add On Close to the Date

Every MEG package, wedding sized ones included, can be extended with add ons: a projector and projection screen, a professional smoke machine, extra microphones, a premium acrylic lectern, modular stage platforms, and additional live technician hours. None of these are locked to the original booking. You can ask for any of them close to the date, and we will tell you the same day whenever we can whether it is still available. What changes near the date is not what you can ask for, it is how quickly we can confirm it: an add on requested a month out has a wide pool of stock and technician time to draw from, one requested inside the 24 hour window is checked against exactly what is still free that day, no more.

## Date and Postponement Changes After Booking

If your wedding date changes after booking, reach out as soon as it does and we confirm whether the new date is available for the package and technician you booked. What "confirm availability" actually risks is worth spelling out. The Wedding Pack and the MICE Pack are the only two packages in our catalog with a live technician built in, and there is no bench of spare technicians waiting for a reassignment: the person committed to your original date may already be booked on the new one. Peak wedding season on the Costa del Sol, spring through early autumn, is also when Saturdays sell out first, so postponing into that window carries a real chance the exact date you want is already taken by another booking. There is no documented rush fee for handling a date change. There is also no guaranteed slot, an honest tradeoff, not a sales pitch. The same 24 hour minimum applies to reconfirming the new date, same as any other booking.

## A Weather Driven Indoor to Outdoor Swap

A late swap between an indoor hall and an outdoor setting changes what the AV setup actually needs, not just where it sits. Outdoor sound has to account for wind, open air coverage, and often a venue curfew that an indoor hall's own walls and acoustics do not impose. Power access can differ too, an outdoor ceremony space does not always have the same outlets a ballroom or finca hall already has wired in. We cover the setup differences in full in our [indoor wedding rental essentials](/blog/indoor-wedding-rental-essentials/) and [outdoor wedding rental considerations](/blog/outdoor-wedding-rental-considerations/) guides. Here, the point that matters for a late change is the same one that applies everywhere else in this guide: a weather driven swap is subject to whether our system can still be configured for the new setting that day, and to the 24 hour minimum, same as a guest count change or a new add on. For what changing weather actually risks on the AV equipment itself, wireless mic moisture, cabling safety, PA and LED heat, see our [weather considerations for outdoor rentals](/blog/weather-considerations-for-outdoor-rentals/) guide.

