## Booking and Service Area

Every booking and every change to one needs at least 24 hours' notice. There is no separate cutoff for changes, and no fee for requesting one, only the same availability check every booking gets. If you have not booked yet, our [when to book wedding AV rentals](/blog/timeline-for-booking-wedding-rentals/) guide covers the first booking timeline, and our [how to choose wedding rentals](/blog/how-to-choose-wedding-rentals/) guide walks through picking between the Eco Pack and the Wedding Pack by guest count. Once your setup is locked in, our [making the most of your wedding rentals](/blog/making-the-most-of-wedding-rentals/) guide covers briefing the technician on your run of show ahead of the day.

## Conclusion

Most late changes to a wedding AV booking with MEG are possible. None of them skip the 24 hour minimum notice, and none of them are guaranteed until we confirm equipment and, where relevant, technician availability against your actual date. Reach out as soon as your guest count, add ons, date, or venue setting changes, the earlier you do, the more of that availability is still there to work with. [Contact us](/contact/) to check what is possible for your date.

## FAQs

### What is MEG's minimum notice policy for changes to an existing booking?

The same 24 hour minimum that applies to every new booking applies to every change to one. All event gear rentals and technical services must be contracted, or reconfirmed, with at least 24 hours' advance notice to guarantee scheduling and logistical availability.

### What happens if my guest count crosses 50 or 80 guests after I've booked?

Crossing from the [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/)'s 50 guest capacity or the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/)'s 80 guest capacity is a package change, not a quantity you add to. It is subject to whether the higher capacity system, and a technician if needed, are still available for your date, and it is still bound by the 24 hour minimum.

### Can I add a projector, smoke machine, or extra technician hours close to my wedding date?

Yes. A projector and screen, a professional smoke machine, extra microphones, a premium acrylic lectern, modular stage platforms, and additional live technician hours can all be requested close to the date. Each is confirmed against real stock and technician availability at the time you ask, not guaranteed automatically.

### What happens if I need to change my wedding date after booking?

[Contact us](/contact/) as soon as the date changes and we confirm whether the new date is available for your package and technician. The Wedding Pack and MICE Pack technicians are not interchangeable on request, and peak season Saturdays sell out first, so a postponement into that window can mean your new date is already booked.

### What if the weather forces a swap between an indoor and outdoor venue?

A late indoor to outdoor swap is treated like any other change: subject to whether our AV setup can be reconfigured for the new setting on your date, and to the 24 hour minimum. See our [indoor](/blog/indoor-wedding-rental-essentials/) and [outdoor](/blog/outdoor-wedding-rental-considerations/) wedding rental guides for what each setting actually needs.

### Do I get a discount if my guest count drops after booking?

No. Package prices are fixed, and there is no documented option to remove an included item or downsize a guest count for a lower rate. Our [tips for reducing wedding rental costs](/blog/tips-for-reducing-wedding-rental-costs/) guide covers the real, honest cost levers, right sizing your package before you book is one of them.
